  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preparation and Mobilization of Migrant Workers from El Salvador to Canada</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upon the request of Maple Leaf Foods in Canada and the Government of El Salvador, IOM will work to coordinate the preparation and deployment of 50 Salvadoran workers to Canada. The process includes pre-departure orientation, health check, English language basic training, visa applications, travel arrangements and certain integration and initial transnational communication services for the migrant workers to be hired by Maple Leaf Foods for employment in their Canadian plants in Brandon (Manitoba). IOM has joined this initiative as a partner in selection schemes to prevent unfair practices related to foreign worker recruitment. The overall objective of the initiative is to contribute to supporting regular, organised, and transparent labour migration schemes in El Salvador, in cooperation with the Ministry of Labour and Foreign Affairs.</narrative>
  </description>
